WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.500
Priorities need to be communicated, not just privately understood.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:12.200
When priorities are invisible, other people cannot align scope, deadlines, requests, or expectations.

3
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.260
Clear communication makes tradeoffs discussable.

4
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:23.760
It allows a person to say, this is the current focus, this is what will wait, this is the deadline risk, and this is what would need to change if a new request becomes more important.

5
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.640
Saying no or not yet is part of responsible work management.

6
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.980
A no does not have to be dismissive.

7
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:39.680
It can be a tradeoff statement: I can take this on if we move that deadline, reduce that scope, reassign that task, or agree that the current priority changes.

8
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.980
Silent acceptance creates hidden multitasking and often produces disappointment later.

9
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:53.660
Boundary management protects attention, focus time, commitments, and recovery from uncontrolled demand.

10
00:00:53.760 --> 00:01:02.880
Boundaries include meeting discipline, response expectations, office hours, escalation paths, and visible focus blocks.

11
00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.500
A boundary should clarify how collaboration still happens.

12
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.600
The point is not to disappear.

13
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.340
The point is to prevent every request from becoming an immediate interruption by default.

14
00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.860
Respecting other people's attention is a professional resource practice.

15
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:23.000
Before scheduling a meeting, ask whether the purpose is clear and whether the right people are involved.

16
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.260
Before sending an urgent message, ask whether it is truly urgent.

17
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.680
Before interrupting focus, ask what cost the interruption creates.

18
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:38.020
Good communication reduces the need for multitasking because it lowers uncertainty and prevents avoidable churn.
